 1299:     check "sgi_re randompixel rows green" "$(count "$RANDLOG" " ok$")"   "8"
 1300:     check "sgi_re randompixel rows red"   "$(count "$RANDLOG" " FAIL$")" "0"
 1301: fi
 1302: 
 1303: #  ------------------------------------------------------------ #505 sgirergbroundtrip
 1304: #  horrible_getputpixel()'s RGB GET read buf[1..3] while its RGB PUT writes the three channels at
 1305: #  buf[0..2] and an explicit pad at buf[3] -- so an RGB pixel did not survive its own round trip and
 1306: #  the red channel was dropped.  RGB was the ONLY 32-bit colour mode in the file failing this way.
 1307: #
 1308: #  THE ARM WAS CHOSEN ON EVIDENCE FROM A DIFFERENT DEVICE, which is what makes the warrant
 1309: #  non-circular: dev_sgi_gbe.c's scanout reads the same tile memory back as
 1310: #  (buf[0]<<24)+(buf[1]<<16)+(buf[2]<<8)+buf[3], and CRMFB_MODE_TYP_RGB8 takes R,G,B from bits
 1311: #  31..24 / 23..16 / 15..8 -- byte 0 is R and byte 3 is UNUSED.  The pad sits at buf[3] because the
 1312: #  CONSUMER ignores buf[3], not because PUT writes a zero there.
 1313: #
 1314: #  `rgb depth64' IS NOT DECORATION -- IT CLOSES A MEASURED CLAUSE-(d) FLOOR BREACH.  The first kill
 1315: #  table's M6_cond (guard kept, repair conditioned on `bufdepth == 4') scored a CLEAN SWEEP 6/6,
 1316: #  because every session then used BUFDEPTH_32 and the mutant's fix branch was the only one the
 1317: #  detector ever executed.  Its mirror M7_cond8 (exempting bufdepth 8 instead) also dies, so the
 1318: #  WIDTH AXIS is closed rather than the one cell the mutant happened to use.
 1319: #
 1320: #  `rgb samemode' reaches the RGB *PUT* arm, which no other row executes -- every other session is
 1321: #  RGB->RGBA.  Measured, not assumed: M8_put corrupts that arm alone and reds exactly this row.
 1322: RGBLOG=$LOGDIR/sgi_re_rgb.log
 1323: python3 sgi_re_rgb_probe.py "$PMAX" gate > "$RGBLOG" 2>&1 || true
 1324: 
 1325: if ! grep -q "SGIRGB_DONE" "$RGBLOG"; then
 1326:     check "sgi_re rgb probe completed" "no" "yes"
 1327: else
 1328:     check "sgi_re rgb probe completed" "yes" "yes"
 1329:     check "sgi_re rgb witness verdict" "$(count "$RGBLOG" '^SGIRGB_WITNESS=PASS$')" "1"
 1330:     #  TWO SPACES AFTER $v, NOT ONE -- the sibling blocks above were both bitten by the one-space
 1331:     #  form, in both of its directions.  Pre-flighted mechanically for this row set before the gate
 1332:     #  ever ran: no name is a prefix of another, and every pattern matches exactly one rendered row.
 1333:     #
 1334:     #  The probe prints names with "%-16s" plus an explicit space, so a name of N chars is followed
 1335:     #  by (16-N)+1 spaces.  The longest here is `rgb not corrupt' at 15, leaving exactly two -- ONE
 1336:     #  CHARACTER of margin.  If a name must grow past 15, widen the probe's "%-16s" in the same diff.
 1337:     #
 1338:     #  *** WHAT A TOO-LONG NAME ACTUALLY DOES: IT REDS, LOUDLY.  The sibling block above says it
 1339:     #  "silently stops testing anything while staying green", and an earlier draft of THIS block
 1340:     #  copied that sentence.  It is WRONG, and the pass-2 panel caught it. ***  `count' returns 0
 1341:     #  when the pattern matches nothing, `check' compares that 0 against a wanted "1", and 0 != 1
 1342:     #  FAILS.  Measured over rendered rows at lengths 15/16/17: 15 matches (ok), 16 and 17 match

codex
The saved logs support the headline scores, and all three edits appear correct within their stated scope. I’ve found further gaps: Alpha never saves the second context to check that zero flags replaced the first context’s flags, and RGB’s “full space” uses only TLB_A and LIN_A. A new `#508` block appeared during inspection; I’m keeping this review focused on `#505–507` and separating incidental findings.
